Let's denote a function

![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/ccd6b10105ec02e1e62a5b638601921c152f8d05.png)

You are given an array $*a*$ consisting of $*n*$ integers. You have to calculate the sum of $*d*(*a*_{*i*}, *a*_{*j*})$ over all pairs $(*i*, *j*)$ such that $1 ≤ *i* ≤ *j* ≤ *n*$.

## Input

The first line contains one integer $*n*$ ($1 ≤ *n* ≤ 200000$) — the number of elements in $*a*$.

The second line contains $*n*$ integers $*a*_{1}$, $*a*_{2}$, ..., $*a*_{*n*}$ ($1 ≤ *a*_{*i*} ≤ 10^{9}$) — elements of the array.

## Output

Print one integer — the sum of $*d*(*a*_{*i*}, *a*_{*j*})$ over all pairs $(*i*, *j*)$ such that $1 ≤ *i* ≤ *j* ≤ *n*$.

## Note

In the first example:

1. $*d*(*a*_{1}, *a*_{2}) = 0$;
2. $*d*(*a*_{1}, *a*_{3}) = 2$;
3. $*d*(*a*_{1}, *a*_{4}) = 0$;
4. $*d*(*a*_{1}, *a*_{5}) = 2$;
5. $*d*(*a*_{2}, *a*_{3}) = 0$;
6. $*d*(*a*_{2}, *a*_{4}) = 0$;
7. $*d*(*a*_{2}, *a*_{5}) = 0$;
8. $*d*(*a*_{3}, *a*_{4}) =  - 2$;
9. $*d*(*a*_{3}, *a*_{5}) = 0$;
10. $*d*(*a*_{4}, *a*_{5}) = 2$.
